                <pb facs="0223" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg115"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received January 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson telegraphs that the American vessels will be convoyed to the dock by
                    the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Detroit</hi>, and that a general engagement
                    may follow if she is fired upon, as she is ready to return the fire.</p>
            </div>
